  "contract_version": "1.1.0-draft",
  "description": "Section 4, both halves. On the way IN: a legacy id key is accepted only because dependencies carries the mapping, and it is translated to the canonical name key and then DROPPED — the vector asserts the exact key set, because an id left lying beside the name makes the node's hash instance-specific and the same workflow exported from two instances would never come back equal to itself. On the way OUT: the value on the wire MUST be the portable identity — the integration's SLUG — never the exporting instance's display name, which here differs from it on purpose. What a product stores in between is its own business.",
